config BR2_PACKAGE_GLIBC_COMPAT
	bool "glibc-compat"
	depends on BR2_TOOLCHAIN_USES_MUSL
	help
	  ABI shim for vendor binaries linked against libc.so.6 (glibc) that
	  must run on a musl rootfs. Provides a libglibc-compat.so with the
	  glibc-only entry points (__xstat, __isoc99_sscanf, ...) that musl
	  does not export, plus rootfs symlinks for libc.so.6 / libm.so.6 /
	  ld-linux.so.3 -> musl libc.

	  Used by Hi3520DV200 (vendor MPP for V200 only ships glibc-linked
	  .so, while glibc cannot run on the SoC's 3.0.8 kernel) and by the
	  SigmaStar infinity3 (MSC313E) SDK libs.

	  The executable that loads the vendor libs links
	  -lglibc-compat-static (their mmap passes a 32-bit off_t) and
	  -lglibc-compat ahead of libc: musl has its own __xstat family,
	  and the first library in load order wins.

	  A call neither can bridge for both ABIs at once (lseek's 32-bit
	  off_t) is redirected per vendor library at install time with
	  rename-import.py, to a glibc-compat wrapper of the same name
	  length.
